## Canonical ownership and registry closure

- `omega_contracts` owns the canonical conductor `OperatorManifestV1`, `GaugeBindingV1`, `OperatorRegistryV1`, typed input/output, capability, permission, witness, and runtime-profile types.
- `omega_state` imports those semantic types and owns only bounded execution, independent evaluation, replay, terminal routing, and receipts.
- `omega_operator_algebra::registry::DeclaredAction` remains the mathematical action-registry owner; no duplicate mathematical semantic type was introduced.
- Unknown fields and unknown enum variants fail serde decoding; lists are strictly sorted and unique; duplicate or unknown owners fail validation.

The admitted registry has one manifest and two bindings:

| Binding | Runtime | Execution | Network | Credentials | Hidden context |
|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| `binding:fixture-canonical-json-echo-v1` | fixture | deterministic fixture | false | false | none |
| `binding:codex-model-fixture-replay-v1` | Codex canned profile | model fixture replay | false | false | none |

The Codex profile is fixture data, not a live model call. Both bindings preserve the same semantic contract, capabilities, permission ceiling, exact writes, witness set, evidence ceiling, typed output, and `AuthorityEffect::None`.

