| packet/source/observer/identity/authority tamper | typed refusal or invalid | PASS |
| producer metadata/run identity/output/write/authority or classification tamper | independent evaluator rejection | PASS |
| deterministic replay and byte-stable fixtures | exact equality | PASS |

## GTOC-2 review repair

Gemini Code Assist review on merged PR #1113 identified a medium-severity diagnostic defect: local GTOC-2 serialization failures were wrapped as `Gtoc1Dependency`, which incorrectly mapped them to terminal `Invalid` and left `Gtoc2Error::Json` unused.

S02-001 preserves canonical JSON bytes while separating provenance. `Gtoc1Error::Json` produced by a local GTOC-2 serialization operation is now converted to `Gtoc2Error::Json` and terminal `InfrastructureFailure`; genuine GTOC-1 classification/validation errors remain `Gtoc1Dependency` and terminal `Invalid`. A serializer that deliberately returns an error proves the route. Successful S01-003 packet, observer, fixture, classification, and receipt bytes remain unchanged.

